  "what_the_environment_seed_changes": "The seed sets NumPy's global generator in the simulator process; it is set anew before every episode's reset. The start state then overwrites the joint positions and velocities of the scene. What the seed still decides is what the reset draws that is not part of that state: the benchmark places its fixtures (cabinet, stove, rack) at every reset within the ranges of the task's file, 1-2 cm. A fresh environment's first seeded reset always gives the same placement; a later reset of the same environment gives it in most tasks but not in all. So every reset's placement is compared with the scene's first, and the environment is built anew when it differs: every episode of a task starts from the same placement, whatever was run before it."
